"Enable 3D" is back in the 3D menu: the viewer's own switch for every picture it shows, for the session, as it was
before +stereo3d10 (where it had become the file's "Not 3D"). It is the stereo layer's Stereo::Enable3DAction, in the
same words as every program on the layer (ORDER 551c); off, every picture is shown flat and nothing is declared, and
no file's choice changes. Alt+Shift+N switches it again.

A file's own "Not 3D", one file's input correction kept in the shared per-file store for every program, stays in the
layer's menu, "3D Input Format". It now also wins over the viewer's one-eye views, which cut such a file in half.

Built against libstereo-layer-dev 1.19.2.
